===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[surroundings]] of, and influences on, a particular item of interest.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Jonathan Rauch|title=Tunnel Vision: The Dawn of Microgovernment|magazine=National Journal|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120306010527/https://www.jonathanrauch.com/jrauch_articles/microgovernment_rules_without_reason/|date=1998-09-19|passage=What was seen from the top down, as a large '''environment''' with many difficult trade-offs, is instead seen from the bottom up--as 10 million microenvironments, each to be regulated in its own right. It is this inversion of perspective that distinguishes microgovernment from other kinds of regulation, and that accounts for its often-bizarre behavior.}}
# The natural world or [[ecosystem]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-06-07|author=David Simpson
|volume=188|issue=26|page=36|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|url=http://www.guardian.co.uk/books/2013/may/18/falling-upwards-richard-holmes-review|title=Fantasy of navigation
|passage=It is tempting to speculate about the incentives or compulsions that might explain why anyone would take to the skies in [the] basket [of a balloon]:&nbsp;[&hellip;]; &nbsp;[&hellip;]; or perhaps to muse on the irrelevance of the borders that separate nation states and keep people from understanding their shared '''environment'''.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261013065245/https://www.theguardian.com/books/2013/may/18/falling-upwards-richard-holmes-review|archivedate=13 October 2026}}
# All the elements that affect a system or its inputs and outputs.
# A particular [[political]] or [[social]] setting, [[arena]] or condition.
# {{lb|en|computing}} The [[software]] or [[hardware]] existing on any particular [[computer]] [[system]].
#: {{ux|en|That [[program]] uses the Microsoft Windows '''environment'''.}}
# {{lb|en|programming}} The set of [[identifiers]] in a [[function|function's]] [[scope]] and their [[bindings]] at that point.
# {{lb|en|computing}} The set of [[variable]]s and their [[value]]s in a [[namespace]] that an [[operating system]] associates with a [[process]].

